# Build context is platform/console. Keep it small and keep host state out.
#
# node_modules is the important one. It exists on the developer machine, it is
# ~90 MB, and copying it in would (a) make every build upload it and (b) shadow
# the clean `npm ci` tree from the deps stage with whatever happens to be on
# that laptop -- including a package installed by hand and never committed. The
# image must be reproducible from package-lock.json alone.
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log
**/.npm

# Test output written by the three harnesses. Regenerated, machine-specific,
# and one of them records absolute paths from the machine that ran it.
prototype/tests/sandbox-last-run.json
prototype/tests/stress-last-run.json
prototype/tests/*.png

# Local dev leftovers
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Nothing in the image needs git history or editor state.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.vscode
**/.idea
